room The Isle of Crete "The bronze coast. \nA place of ruin.\nA place of desolation.\nHusks of broken ships litter the horizon. \nNothing moves but the distant hulk of a giant, mindlessly hurling rocks at birds and ships out at sea."

    scenery sea "Water laps listlessly at the shore. A grey sky weighs heavy above."

    scenery bronze coast "The grooves of the giant's steps wearying the stone in endless circumference, since before time."

    scenery ruin, desolation, husks, ships "Flat. Desolate. A world broken in lifeless routine."
    scenery Eris "Gods come and go as they please. Eris seldom lingers."

    person Talos "Bronze sentinel,\nforged protector of its land,\npaces the extent of its limited horizon."

        on give with Brass Lantern:
            say "Talos lost in thought searches the horizon for a ship to dare his vigilant eye."
            say "Then after a long silence Talos speaks in a wavering voice, hollow and dead:"
            say "Not being."
            say "Not reflection."
            say "No wisdom."
            say "No light."
            #move player to 

    on turn 1:
        say "They say Eris drops apples like an orchard in fall."
        say "But that day she appeared in a hiss of carbon dioxide"
        say "and dropped a brass lantern at Medea's feet."
        move Brass Lantern to location.

    on turn 2:
        say "Uh oh, the giant is coming this way."

    on turn 3:
        say "You feel the tremor of the earth with his every step."

    on turn 4:
        say "WHOOO… AARE… YOOOU…? Talos voice booms, reverberating through the emptiness." 
        say "With a grinding of gears the giant comes to a halt."
        move Talos to location.

    on turn 5-:
        say "Talos glowers down on you."

test "default"
    x me. "sorceress"
    take lamp. "taken"
    x lamp. "dark"
    x coast. "grooves"
    x ruin. "Desolate"
    x talos. "sentinel"
    give lamp to talos. "not being"